{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy gives clear states a forward-progress bias, routes every obstacle event through a dedicated recovery state, uses backward motion only for front-obstacle escape, prefers directed turns away from side obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately on path_clear. Action states self-loop on non-critical path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant sensing availability from motion capability so specifications can impose the task policy cleanly.",
    "Use one policy automaton with perception and one-shot action states, plus a small liveness-bias automaton to prefer move_forward over random_walk in sustained clear conditions."
  ],
